* [CRITICAL] LOGIC TruncateWithEllipsis does not enforce maxLen for small values (at truncateWithEllipsis)
  - Issue: When maxLen ≤ 3, `slice(0, maxLen - 3)` uses a negative end index, causing the result to exceed maxLen. For example, `truncateWithEllipsis("abcde", 2)` returns `"abcd..."` (length 7) instead of a 2‑character string, violating the function’s contract.
  - Fix: Guard the ellipsis length before slicing:
    ```js
    const ellipsis = "...";
    if (maxLen <= ellipsis.length) {
      return ellipsis.slice(0, maxLen);
    }
    if (text.length < maxLen) return text;
    return text.slice(0, maxLen - ellipsis.length) + ellipsis;
    ```

* [CRITICAL] LOGIC LastNLines off‑by‑one and mishandles edge cases (at lastNLines)
  - Issue: `lines.slice(lines.length - n - 1)` drops an extra line, so `lastNLines(text, 0)` returns the last line instead of an empty string, and `lastNLines(text, n)` for `n > lines.length` returns all lines. When `n === lines.length`, the result is empty, breaking the expected “last N lines” semantics.
  - Fix: Compute the start index safely and slice from there:
    ```js
    const lines = text.split("\n");
    const start = Math.max(0, lines.length - n);
    return lines.slice(start).join("\n");
    ```
